# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Finance — configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in only what you want. `.env*` is
# git-ignored. EVERY key below is optional: with none of them set, the
# dashboard, the CLI, planning, taxes, spreadsheet import and XLSX export all
# work against the local database. Keys only add sync and AI.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#   bun run fin doctor        # prints which of these are configured, locally
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# libSQL / SQLite connection string. The default is a single file in the repo
# root and is what every script, the CLI and the web app fall back to.
# `bin/fin` pins this to the repo's own file so your shell's working directory
# never decides which ledger you are reading.
DATABASE_URL=file:finance.db


# ── Bank sync (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SimpleFIN Bridge — read-only account + transaction + holdings sync.
# Get a setup token at https://bridge.simplefin.org ($1.50/month or $15/year).
# Paste EITHER value here; both are secrets.
#
#   • Setup token — a long base64 string. Claimed automatically on the first
#     sync, and the resulting access URL is cached in the database.
#     Setup tokens are SINGLE-USE: if yours was already claimed, generate a new
#     one rather than re-pasting it.
#   • Access URL  — https://USER:PASSWORD@beta-bridge.simplefin.org/simplefin
#
# Without this, use CSV import on the Accounts page or add accounts manually.
# SIMPLEFIN_ACCESS_URL=


# ── AI providers (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlocks: AI categorisation of merchants that no rule or cache entry matches,
# the natural-language cash box, and the research assistant (`fin research`,
# the Research page). Categorisation and the cash box try providers in order
# (Anthropic → OpenAI → NVIDIA NIM) and fall back to deterministic rules if
# all of them fail. The research assistant uses exactly one provider per run
# and never falls through to another vendor.

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5              # default if unset

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                      # default if unset

# NVIDIA NIM — https://build.nvidia.com (free tier via the Developer Program)
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# NIM_API_KEY=                                  # accepted as an alias
# NIM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b                  # default if unset; must honour tool_choice
# NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1   # default if unset


# ── Research assistant data sources (optional) ───────────────────────────────
# Only used by the research assistant's tools. Neither ever receives your
# personal financial data: the market-data tool sends a ticker symbol, and the
# search tool sends a fixed query template built from a ticker or a tax topic.

# Alpha Vantage — quotes, company overviews, statements, earnings, news,
# insider trades. Free tier is 25 requests/day.
# https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
# ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# Exa — public-source search, restricted to sec.gov for filings and irs.gov
# for tax topics. https://dashboard.exa.ai/api-keys
# EXA_API_KEY=
# EXASEARCH_API_KEY=                            # accepted as an alias


# ── Set for you ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FINANCE_DEMO=1 renders the "fictional household" banner. `bun run demo` sets
# it; you should not need it in this file.
# FINANCE_DEMO=

# NODE_ENV is set by the framework (`development` under `next dev`,
# `production` under `next build`/`next start`). Do not set it here.
